				<r3d:description language="eng">The Network for the Detection of Atmospheric Composition Change (NDACC), a major contributor to the worldwide atmospheric research effort, consists of a set of globally distributed research stations providing consistent, standardized, long-term measurements of atmospheric trace gases, particles, spectral UV radiation reaching the Earth&#039;s surface, and physical parameters, centered around the following priorities.</r3d:description>
